[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marin-community/marin/issues/comments/4726762768","html_url":"https://github.com/marin-community/marin/issues/6442#issuecomment-4726762768","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marin-community/marin/issues/6442","id":4726762768,"node_id":"IC_kwDOLj5faM8AAAABGbytEA","user":{"login":"ClassicLarry","id":42926649,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyOTI2NjQ5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/42926649?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ClassicLarry","html_url":"https://github.com/ClassicLarry","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ClassicLarry/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ClassicLarry/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ClassicLarry/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ClassicLarry/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ClassicLarry/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ClassicLarry/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ClassicLarry/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ClassicLarry/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ClassicLarry/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-17T06:36:01Z","updated_at":"2026-06-17T06:36:01Z","body":"🤖 Added a sixth variant for the norm-ablation series — moves from the **embed**-input norms to the **MLP**-input norm inside each block.\n\n### F. \\`moe_may_mlp_no_rms\\` ([branch](https://github.com/marin-community/marin/tree/moe_may_mlp_no_rms))\n\n\\`model.py\\`: \\`GrugModelConfig.mlp_skip_rms_norm: bool = False\\`. When True, the per-block pre-MLP RMSNorm (\\`rms_mlp\\`) is dropped so the MLP input is just \\`mlp_gated_norm(x)\\` (per-dim GatedNorm alone). Tests whether GatedNorm by itself is sufficient pre-MLP normalization.\n\nLaunchers:\n- \\`experiments/grug/moe/moe_may_compute_opt_d512_ep1_mlp_no_rms.py\\`\n- \\`experiments/grug/moe/moe_may_compute_opt_d768_ep1_mlp_no_rms.py\\`\n\nSubmitted on v5p-8 us-east5-a interactive:\n- d=512: \\`/larry/iris-run-job-20260617-063537\\`\n- d=768: \\`/larry/iris-run-job-20260617-063546\\`","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marin-community/marin/issues/comments/4726762768/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marin-community/marin/issues/comments/4726787036","html_url":"https://github.com/marin-community/marin/issues/6442#issuecomment-4726787036","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marin-community/marin/issues/6442","id":4726787036,"node_id":"IC_kwDOLj5faM8AAAABGb0L3A","user":{"login":"ClassicLarry","id":42926649,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyOTI2NjQ5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/42926649?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ClassicLarry","html_url":"https://github.com/ClassicLarry","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ClassicLarry/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ClassicLarry/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ClassicLarry/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ClassicLarry/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ClassicLarry/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ClassicLarry/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ClassicLarry/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ClassicLarry/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ClassicLarry/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-17T06:39:40Z","updated_at":"2026-06-17T06:39:40Z","body":"🤖 Equal-tps speedup table for variants A–E (all finished except E d=768 which crashed at ~90% budget). F (mlp_no_rms) is still running; will update when it lands.\n\nMethod: per the speedup formula in \\`agent.md\\`, refit the scaling-law coefficient \\`A_bl\\` through the baseline (loss, budget) point, invert to find \\`C_needed\\` for the variant loss, then report \\`C_needed / budget\\` (i.e., how much more compute the baseline would need to match the variant loss). Throughput is factored out, so this isolates the loss gain from any hardware/throughput differences.\n\nBaselines: \\`moe_may_compute_opt_d512_ep1\\` (3.5422 @ 3.16e17 FLOPs), \\`moe_may_compute_opt_d768_ep1\\` (3.2273 @ 1.81e18 FLOPs).\n\n| variant | d=512 loss | d=512 spdup | d=768 loss | d=768 spdup |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| baseline | 3.5422 | 1.000 | 3.2273 | 1.000 |\n| **A** embed_late_decay | 3.5418 | 1.002 | 3.2231 | 1.028 |\n| **B** embed_no_rms | 3.5355 | 1.037 | 3.2189 | **1.056** |\n| **C** embed_no_norms | 3.5862 | **0.788** | 3.2592 | **0.814** |\n| **D** embed_only_rms | 3.5343 | **1.044** | 3.2211 | 1.041 |\n| **E** embed_no_rms_late_decay50 | 3.5353 | 1.038 | — | crashed @ ~90% |\n| **F** mlp_no_rms | (running) | — | (running) | — |\n\nReads:\n- **C (drop both norms) is clearly worse.** At d=768 the baseline only needs ~81% as much compute to match it — dropping the GatedNorm without anything in front of it hurts.\n- **B and D are the winners**, but they cross over: at d=512 the RMSNorm-only path (D) is slightly better (1.044× vs 1.037×); at d=768 the GatedNorm-only path (B) takes the lead (1.056× vs 1.041×). Either norm alone helps; running both looks like mild overkill.\n- **A (late-decay LR)** is small but real at d=768 (+2.8%); negligible at d=512.\n- **E ≈ B at d=512** — the late-decay add-on doesn't move the needle on top of dropping the RMSNorm.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marin-community/marin/issues/comments/4726787036/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":